# GitHub Actions — PR cadence

GitHub Free public repos cap concurrent jobs at 20. Verify is `unit` plus **eight** e2e shards (9 jobs per ready PR). Two ready PRs use 18 jobs — stay **below** 20 so merge-time `main` Verify and Preview can start. Nine e2e shards would fill the cap (2 × 10) with no headroom. **Ready** PRs consume that pool; **drafts** do not (`.github/workflows/verify.yml` skips draft jobs).

## Stay draft until local verify

- Open PRs as draft. Keep them draft through intermediate commits.
- Local `pnpm verify` is the inner gate. Do not poll Actions after every push.

## Mark ready once — only if a slot is free

- Mark ready only after local `pnpm verify` passes **and** fewer than **2** non-draft PRs already target `main`.
- Count with `gh pr list --base main --state open` (ignore drafts). Do not count `main`'s own Verify.
- Do not mark ready on the first push, then keep pushing. Each later synchronize cancels in-progress Verify and starts a new e2e.

```text
# ❌ BAD — ready immediately, five more pushes, wait on Actions while still editing
# ❌ BAD — mark ready when two non-draft PRs already target main
# ✅ GOOD — draft until pnpm verify is green, mark ready once if a slot is free
```

## At most 2 non-draft PRs — no slot, stop

Before marking ready, count open non-draft PRs targeting `main`. If that count is already **2**, **stop**:

- Leave this PR **draft**.
- Do **not** mark ready, merge, poll, or wait for a slot.
- End the session. Summary: work is complete; draft is waiting; a human will mark it ready. That is success, not a blocker.

A human owns the queue. Only an explicit “mark ready now” overrides the cap.

Do not use larger GitHub runners to raise the cap. See [github-actions-standard-runners.mdc](github-actions-standard-runners.mdc).
